Personal Context is a &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; capability that distinguishes &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI from other chatbots like Claude and OpenAI. &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; has access to the data on your iPhone, from emails and messages to photos and files. &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can find anything you're looking for. Apple rebuilt its search index for &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI, and it's more comprehensive for a better search experience.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can see what's on your screen with onscreen awareness, and answer questions about what you're looking at. If there's an image on Instagram and you want to know where it was taken, you can just ask &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; where it was taken and get a response. <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/visual-intelligence/">Visual Intelligence</a> is now part of the Camera app, and &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can answer questions about anything you take a picture of.<br/>
<br/>
Like other chatbots, &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can search the web and access general world knowledge, so it can provide responses to any questions you might have. It can evaluate documents, solve math problems, craft recipes, walk you through DIY tasks, help you plan a party, and more.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can take action in and across apps, getting detailed maps directions with multiple stops, editing and sharing photos, or writing an email from scratch in your own writing style. It can do multiple tasks that are included in the same request.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; is located in the iPhone's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a>, and there's a glassy new &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; bubble with bright colors that pops up when &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; is activated. You can use Hey &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; or hold down the side button, but &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; also comes up with a swipe down from the top center of the display. Responses show up in that same area, and if you swipe on a response, you can get more information and ask follow-up questions.<br/>
<br/>
Apple also created a full &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; app where you can revisit past conversations and start a new conversation. The &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; app syncs across devices, so you can start a conversation on your iPhone and wrap it up on your Mac. &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI is available in &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;, &zwnj;iPadOS 27&zwnj;, &zwnj;macOS Golden Gate&zwnj;, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/watchos-27/">watchOS 27</a>, and visionOS 27, plus it works on AirPods and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/carplay/">CarPlay</a>.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI has the same device requirements as <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a>, so you'll need an iPhone 15 Pro or later to use it. &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI is available in beta right now, and Apple is still refining. &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; is limited to developers, with a public beta set to come out in July. &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; with &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI will launch in September.<div class="linkback">Related Roundups: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipados-27/">iPadOS 27</a></div><div class="linkback">Tag: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/10/ios-27-siri-ai-hands-on/">Hands-On With iOS 27&#039;s Siri AI</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/hands-on-with-ios-27s-siri-ai.2483763/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>